# Copy to .sandcastle/.env and fill in. This file is git-ignored.
#
# IMPORTANT: Sandcastle forwards EVERY key in this file into the sandbox, where
# the autonomous agent can read it. Put a credential here only if the agent
# itself needs it. Right now exactly one does.
#
# In particular, never add:
#   VERCEL_TOKEN         — the host needs it to create sandboxes, not the agent.
#                          Export it in your shell instead: `export VERCEL_TOKEN=...`
#   GH_TOKEN             — all GitHub writes happen host-side under your own
#                          `gh` login. The agent never talks to GitHub.
#   ASSEMBLYAI_API_KEY   — production secrets for the deployed app. They belong
#   BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN  in Vercel project environment variables, and an
#                          autonomous agent has no use for them.

# Claude Code auth. Get one with `claude setup-token` — bills against your
# existing subscription rather than opening a metered API account.
CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=
